# Commits that `git blame` should skip: bulk, behaviour-free changes.
# GitHub reads this file on its own. Locally, once per clone:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
# One full 40-character commit hash per line, with a comment above it.
#
# Only list a commit that changes nothing but formatting or mechanical
# rewrites (e.g. a repo-wide `ruff format`), merged on its own. Use the hash
# as it lands on `main`: a squash merge creates a new one.
